Repair the complete source below and return a corrected complete `solution.rs` using only the standard library. Keep the API unchanged. `qualified_ref(kind, name)` accepts kind `"branch"` or `"tag"` and a nonempty name containing no ASCII whitespace (as defined by Rust `char::is_ascii_whitespace`), colon, or leading slash; it returns the matching `refs/...` mirror mapping or `None`. `project_slug(remote)` removes surrounding ASCII whitespace only (as defined by Rust `char::is_ascii_whitespace`), removes trailing `/` characters, takes the final component after either `/` or `:`, removes exactly one trailing `.git`, and returns a nonempty slug; malformed or empty results return `None`. Non-ASCII whitespace, including U+2003, is ordinary slug content and must remain unchanged. `RepoPlan::tracked_refs` emits the primary branch first, then unique supporting branches in their original order, then unique tags in their original order; invalid entries are skipped, and otherwise identical branch and tag names remain distinct references. Inputs and stored strings must not be mutated.

